  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a strong upward trend followed by high volatility (spikes), the model consistently underestimates the immediate upside and fails to capture subsequent mean reversion, resulting in a systematic negative bias during volatile periods.",
    "The model exhibits significant lag in reacting to sentiment shifts; specifically, it ignores or undervalues positive sentiment signals that precede sharp price increases, leading to persistent under-forecasting when market momentum is high.",
    "In low-sentiment environments with downward volatility, the model tends to overestimate the depth of the decline and fails to account for rapid mean reversion, causing an upward bias in the forecast relative to actual outcomes.",
    "The 30-day horizon consistently underestimates the amplitude of price swings; the model produces a smoother, trend-following path that misses the high-frequency oscillations characteristic of EU ETS markets during transition phases.",
    "When sentiment history contains mixed or low values despite volatile price action, the model defaults to a conservative linear projection, failing to incorporate the stochastic nature of carbon prices which often reverses quickly after initial moves."
  ]
}
